The GC reframe is producing one useful constraint—absence must be treated as incomplete evidence—but it currently overreaches in two technical ways: reachability is not identical to “wanted,” and the set of granted leases is not a collector root set. Those are not terminology nits; they are being used to justify state and correctness claims.
